    {
      "type": "done",
      "answer": "Based on the lecture material, here is a comparison of data parallelism and task parallelism, both of which are forms of parallelism where multiple jobs (instructions, operations, or tasks) are done concurrently [S1].\n\n**Data Parallelism**\n*   **Definition:** Different pieces of data can be operated in parallel [S1].\n*   **Examples:** Vector processing and array processing [S1].\n\n**Task Parallelism**\n*   **Definition:** Different tasks can be operated in parallel [S1].\n*   **Examples:** Multithreading [S1].\n\n**Key Distinction:**\nThe primary difference lies in what is being parallelized:\n*   **Data Parallelism** focuses on applying the same operation to different chunks of data simultaneously.\n*   **Task Parallelism** focuses on executing different, distinct tasks or operations simultaneously.\n\n**Source:**\nThese definitions and examples are found on page 33 of the lecture document [S1].",
      "citations": [
        {
          "document_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402",
          "chunk_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402-p33-1",
          "page": 33,
          "text": "From CPU to GPU: Parallelism for Huge Computing Power!\n  Multiprocessors\n\n¡  Parallelism: Do multiple jobs concurrently.\n\n   ¡  Job: instructions, operations, tasks\n\n\n¡ Data Parallelism\n\n   ¡  Different pieces of data can be operated in parallel\n\n   ¡  Vector processing and array processing\n\n\n¡  Task Parallelism\n\n   ¡  Different tasks can be operated in parallel\n\n   ¡  Multithreading",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402/pages/33/preview",
          "source": "S1"
